# Exports in ntoskrnl.spec that the LoongArch64 ntoskrnl.exe image does not
# define today.
#
# sdk/tools/elf2pe/elf2pe.py builds this image's export directory from the
# spec2def-generated ntoskrnl.def. Every EXPORTS entry must name a symbol the
# linked ELF defines or a forwarder into another module (hal.*); an entry that
# names neither fails the link with the complete list of such names, because an
# export directory that quietly dropped them would promise less than the
# catalog does. This file is the reviewed exception list: the names below are
# left out of the export directory and each omission is printed during the
# link, and every name that is not listed here still fails.
#
# Keep this list shrinking, and remove a line as soon as the symbol appears in
# ntoskrnl.exe.elf; the link then warns that the allow-list entry is unused.
# Of the 192 names below, 181 are defined by an archive member that nothing in
# the kernel references, so the linker never pulls it in (it does not link
# archives whole). The other 11 have no implementation in the link at all:
# KxSaveFloatingPointState/KxRestoreFloatingPointState are the amd64/arm64
# kernel implementations of KeSave/KeRestoreFloatingPointState, and
# RtlVirtualUnwind2/RtlVirtualUnwind/RtlLookupFunctionEntry/RtlUnwind/
# RtlUnwindEx/RtlRestoreContext/RtlGetCallersAddress/__C_specific_handler/
# _local_unwind are the unwind and SEH implementation the LoongArch64 port has
# not written (sdk/lib/rtl/CMakeLists.txt lists no loongarch64/unwind.c).
#
# One export name per line, exactly as it appears in ntoskrnl.def.

